        "side": "new",
        "severity": "low",
        "category": "bug",
        "title": "Search-param-free key built from wrong prefix",
        "explanation": "The search-param-free key is built from `keyPrefix`, which can contain search params, instead of from the `keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams` parameter that was added for this purpose. The result is correct today only because search params appear just in the leaf __PAGE__ segment key. If any non-leaf segment key ever carries search params, the server-side head key will no longer match the prerendered key, and the PPR resume mismatch this change fixes will come back.",
        "suggestion": "Use `keyPrefixWithoutSearchParams + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams` as the fourth argument.",
        "evidence": "      keyPrefix + '/' + cacheKeyWithoutSearchParams",
        "confidence": 0.8,
